{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>and they will listen.</b> Every שמע followed by a lamed or bet, the meaning is that they will hear the matter that the voice carries, not to hear the voice. The dagesh in the Hebrew yod is a mark of eloquence to show the yod of relation, for the yod of the Hebrews in chireq under the resh is a sign of plural. As in the rule of:" "<b>has befallen us.</b> With heh and also with alef the meaning is one, like נקרא נקריתי (II Samuel 1:6). And I will further explain its meaning, for it is פן יפגענו (below, verse 22:3 [5:3])."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 3, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:31:22.184893721Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}